            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for suggestion!\r\n\r\n> Since the items in the dashboard aren't changing all that much (pretty much never), querying for an item becomes a bit cumbersome, as if I had the option to set the shortcut for that item directly would be much more efficient.\r\n\r\nItems can change in start screen, like in default \"Sessions\" and \"Recent files\" sections. If user wants some static item names, the current suggestion is to manually design item names to have unique prefix. \r\n\r\nI would suggest modifying item names by manually prepending them with the hotkey you'd like. Something like this:\r\n\r\n```\r\n- N New File\r\n- G Git status\r\n- F Find File\r\n- R Grep Text\r\n- Q Quit\r\n```\r\n\r\nOr choose entirely different description for problematic entries. I opted for `Live grep` in [`telescope` built-in section](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/09476036cbaa7676172f7dd37a26a51a92388aab/lua/mini/starter.lua#L545).\r\n\r\nSorry, but current approach with querying will be the only possibility in the foreseeable future.",
